.TH RSDEPLOY 1 "2026-08-02" "rsdeploy 1.1.0"
.SH NAME
rsdeploy \- deploy a directory to a remote host with rsync
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rsdeploy
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fB-c\fR \fIconfig\fR] [\fIrsync_args\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rsdeploy
uses
.BR rsync (1)
to synchronize a source directory with a remote destination. It performs a dry
run by default; pass \fB-w\fR to make changes.

Configuration may be provided by environment variables or a \fI.env\fR file.
Without \fB-c\fR, the command searches upward from the current directory for
\fI.env\fR. A configured source path is relative to the directory of the last
loaded configuration file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " file"
Load \fIfile\fR as configuration. May be specified more than once.
.TP
.BI \-d " destination"
Set the remote destination. Overrides \fBRSDEPLOY_DEST\fR.
.TP
.BI \-f " filter"
Use \fIfilter\fR as an rsync merge filter. Overrides \fBRSDEPLOY_FILTER\fR.
.TP
.B \-h
Show usage help.
.TP
.B \-r
Alias for \fB-w\fR.
.TP
.BI \-s " source"
Set the source directory. Overrides \fBRSDEPLOY_SRC\fR.
.TP
.B \-v
Show the command name and version.
.TP
.B \-w
Perform a wet run. Without this option, rsdeploy passes rsync its dry-run flag.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RSDEPLOY_DEST
Remote destination in rsync syntax.
.TP
.B RSDEPLOY_FILTER
Optional rsync filter file.
.TP
.B RSDEPLOY_SRC
Source directory to deploy.
.PP
The legacy \fBDEPLOY_DEST\fR, \fBDEPLOY_FILTER\fR, and \fBDEPLOY_SRC\fR
variables are also accepted from configuration files.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.TP
.B rsync
Copies files to the configured destination.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Preview a deployment using a nearby \fI.env\fR file:
.nf
.B rsdeploy
.fi
.TP
Deploy using an explicit configuration file:
.nf
.B rsdeploy -w -c deploy.env
.fi
.TP
Deploy with values supplied on the command line:
.nf
.B rsdeploy -w -s public -d user@example.com:/var/www/site
.fi
